    <div class="container">
      <div class="dec">
        <h1>DESCRIPTION</h1>
        <p class="decp">
          The Water Alert System is a vital tool for monitoring water levels in various villages, offering timely alerts to ensure community safety. With a user-friendly interface, users, including both normal and admin users, can access current water level information for six different villages. Clickable buttons represent each village, enabling users to view detailed status updates. Color-coded indicators - green for stable conditions, yellow for warnings, and red for flood alerts - provide instant insights into the severity of the situation. This system facilitates proactive decision-making, empowering individuals and authorities to take swift and effective measures in response to fluctuating water levels, enhancing overall community resilience. The system's intuitive interface fosters community engagement by enabling users to access vital information with ease. Through real-time updates and color-coded indicators, individuals can make informed decisions and implement precautionary measures promptly. This proactive approach not only mitigates risks but also fosters a sense of collective responsibility, enhancing community resilience and well-being.
        </p>
      </div>
      <h1>CURRENT WATER LEVEL FOR VILLAGES</h1>

      <div class="sim-banner">
        <strong>What is real here:</strong> rainfall is a live forecast from Open-Meteo for each
        village&rsquo;s actual coordinates, and the AI assessments are real model calls.
        <strong>River levels are simulated</strong> by a hydrograph model
        (<code>lib/hydrology.js</code>) because this project has no physical sensors.
        Severity is decided by an AI agent, then checked against a deterministic threshold rule
        that the model cannot override downwards &mdash; see <code>agents/guardrails.js</code>.
      </div>

      <button class="assess-all" id="assessAll">Run AI assessment for all villages</button>
      <div class="grid">
        <% snapshot.forEach(function (v) { %>
        <div class="village" id="village-<%= v.villageId %>" data-village="<%= v.villageId %>"
             data-initial-severity="<%= v.deterministicSeverity %>">
          <h2><%= v.villageName %></h2>
          <hr />
          <div class="status-circle" data-role="circle"></div>
          <p class="text">Status: <span data-role="status">—</span></p>
          <p class="text">Water Level: <span data-role="level"><%= v.levelCm %></span> cm</p>
          <p class="text">Warning <%= v.warningLevelCm %> cm &middot; Danger <%= v.dangerLevelCm %> cm</p>

          <div class="ai-panel">
            <button class="ai-button" data-role="assess">Run AI assessment</button>
            <div data-role="ai-result" hidden></div>
          </div>

          <button onclick="toggleDetails('<%= v.villageId %>')">View More</button>
        </div>
        <% }); %>
      </div>
        <!-- Include other village divs similarly -->
      </div>
    </div>
   
